[{:seon.task/name "drivers-leave-src"
  :seon.task/plan "Done (2026-10-23, worktree session shrink2): the drivers left src. seon.check, seon.e2e and seon.fixtures are in test/ (outside src's count); the release binary is `jolt build -m seon.main` (220.4 MB, was 238.1 with the driver compiled in): seon.main/-main serves root and ports and, for every other mode, loads the check driver from the checkout's source (seon.main/checkout-roots!: deps.edn roots and test/ and src/ as source roots). A root whose provider's config is :scripted adds the checkout's source before it starts and seon.model/scripted loads :seon.config.ai/script by name (one not found is :seon.model/no-script). The e2e loop's subject, generation, is seon.generation in src (the loop edits Seon's own source). src went 19,304 -> ~17,400 lines. The root's thread roster went with them (`seon.check/declared-threads`, `threads`). Then (worktree drivers-out3): `seon.root/fs-call!` and `agent-stats!` went (check calls `seon.root/call!`, now public, with the request); dead `seon.lib/pipe`, `events` and their defcs went. Left on purpose: `branch-diff` (parity: `my.program/diff`), `seon.root/apply!` and `seon.root/events` (root's REPL surface, tests evaluate them in a root), `seon.lib/gc-stats` (seon.cost calls it). Test-only in src and still owed a decision (notes `src-test-only-vars`): the measure/judge half of `seon.cost`, `seon.source/refresh-tx`, `seon.proofs/step-digests`, `seon.program/graph-index`."
  :seon.task/kind :work
  :seon.task/needs #{"seon.program/definitions-from-the-compiler"}
  :seon.task/proofs #{seon.main-test/root-boots-without-test-fixtures}}
 {:seon.task/name "forks-live-in-one-place"
  :seon.task/plan "What exists: .gitmodules points the submodules into experiment directories (reference-code/jolt -> the prototype folder's jolt/, chez -> e14/chez-share, datahike and konserve -> libs/, persistent-sorted-set -> e4/pss-a, and others), so the ~100 GB of old experiments (l1, l2, pf1, r4, r5, fx1, proto, scratch, perf, l3, x1, e*) cannot be removed without breaking `git submodule update` and clones of next/. Correct (owner 2026-10-23: next becomes the root folder, self-contained; the module store is the home): .gitmodules url ./.git/modules/reference-code/<name> (a relative URL resolves against the superproject when it has no remote, and a clone, and a clone of a clone, resolve into their own .git/modules), after every source branch and copy is a local head or tag in that module (step B, done 2026-10-23); the measurements, the stray branches and the steps are the archived paper self-contained-plan-2026-10-23.md (git history) (steps B and C); then `git submodule sync` in the main tree only; a fresh `git clone --recurse-submodules` of next/ builds (bin/build seon) and bin/check is green. Then the owner deletes the experiment directories (the owner's act; list them with sizes). Also the move plan's precondition (forks pushable from one place)."
  :seon.task/kind :work}
